\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, Thou sovereign Lord of all,
\par The same through one eternal day,
\par Attend Thy feeblest followers' call,
\par And O instruct us how to pray!
\par Pour out the supplicating grace,
\par And stir us up to seek Thy face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We cannot think a gracious thought,
\par We cannot feel a good desire,
\par Till Thou, who call'dst a world  from nought,
\par The power into our hearts ispire:
\par The promised intercessor give,
\par And let us now Thyself recieve.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Come in Thy pleading Spirit down
\par To us who for Thy coming stay;
\par Of all Thy gifts we ask but one,
\par We ask the constant power to pray:
\par Indulge us, Lord, in this request;
\par Thou canst not then deny the rest.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

